Use server-side include/composition instead of iframe.

For view_homepage.tpl, your non-iframe options are:

Native Smarty include (best if same app/context)

Put the programmer page content in a partial (example: _programmer_panel.tpl)
In view_homepage.tpl, do {include file="_programmer_panel.tpl"}
Pros: fastest, shared DOM/CSS/JS, no cross-frame issues.
Render by controller into same template

Have backend assign data ($smarty->assign(...))
Build the programmer section directly in view_homepage.tpl
Pros: clean architecture, easiest permissions/data control.
Client-side fetch + inject (what your header router already does)

Fetch an internal route returning HTML fragment
Parse/extract content and inject into a target div
Re-run needed scripts carefully (you already built this pattern)
Pros: dynamic without full reload.
Cons: script/style collisions, needs strict fragment contract.
AJAX data + client render (preferred over HTML splice long-term)

Expose JSON endpoint for programmer page data
Render UI with JS template/client code in homepage
Pros: most robust, avoids importing foreign page chrome/scripts.
Web component/JS module mounted in homepage

Package programmer section as reusable JS component
Mount into <div id="programmer-host"></div>
Pros: reusable and isolated behavior without iframe.
What to avoid (if replacing iframe)
Full-page HTML fetch/splice from unrelated apps unless necessary.
Bringing external page global CSS/JS into homepage without scoping.
Recommendation for LEAF
Given your existing architecture, do this in order:

Preferred: convert programmer page into a partial tpl + shared backend data and include it in view_homepage.tpl.
If you need async loading: return a fragment endpoint (content-only, no header/footer/scripts) and inject into a host.
Long-term: move to JSON API + client render for stability.
